cellPad: DualShock 3 through SDL3's HIDAPI PS3 drivers: analog button pressure and the main driver's accelerometer centres.
From the Killzone 3 port's 4010 (commits 087439a5, 92419637).
What: SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3 and SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS3_SIXAXIS_DRIVER are set to 1 at SDL_HINT_NORMAL priority (an
environment variable of the same name wins; a [pad] line says which value took effect). A PS3-type pad whose joystick
has all 16 axes gets its ten button pressures from joystick axes 6-15 (cross, circle, square, triangle, L1, R1, up,
down, left, right; (v + 32768) / 257) instead of the digital 0/255 (PadHostState.press_real; cellPadGetData then only
raises a 0 pressure under a set digital bit). The SIXAXIS words of a PS3-type pad are shifted onto SDL's main PS3
driver centres (X 513, Y 511, Z 511; a flat pad reads Y 398) after pad_sdl_sensors.
Why: both SDL PS3 drivers are off by default on Windows and Linux, so a DS3 reached the game only as a generic pad
with 0/255 pressures. Not run on a real DS3 yet (ASSUMPTION marks in pad_host.h). Sorted after 4010 and before 7016.
